                                            BUSINESS QUESTION
Which periods recorded the highest trading activity?

                                QUERY
Yearly trends
SELECT
	EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date) AS highest_trading_year,
	SUM(volume) AS highest_trade
FROM stock_data
GROUP BY
		EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date)
ORDER BY
		highest_trade DESC;

Monthly Trends
SELECT
	EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date) AS highest_trading_month,
	SUM(volume) AS highest_trade
FROM stock_data
GROUP BY
		EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date)
ORDER BY
		highest_trade DESC;


SELECT
	EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date) AS highest_trading_year,
	EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date) AS highest_trading_month,
	SUM(volume) AS highest_trade
FROM stock_data
GROUP BY
		EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date),
		EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date)
ORDER BY
		highest_trade DESC;

                  Insight:
From the first query thats the yearly trends, it shows that 2016 was the highest overall  trading year
While from the second query,it shows that January  is the highest trading month
Now combining the two queries,now the result shows that 2016 January is the highest  trading date,followed by February which is not suppose to be so but because it was linked to the year were trading was high,it became the second trading date
2016 recorded the highest overall trading activity, while January showed the highest monthly trading volume. This suggests stronger investor participation and market activity during those periods.

               Recommendation:
The company should monitor periods with unusually high trading activity because they may indicate major market movements, investor confidence shifts,
